<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuwen Huaji</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 619</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuwen Huaji (died 619) was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a> general who in 618 led the coup at Jiangdu (modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangzhou">Yangzhou</a>) in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang of Sui</a> was strangled. He marched his army north and proclaimed himself emperor of a state called Xu, but was defeated by Li Mi and then captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dou-jiande">Dou Jiande</a>, who executed him in 619.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuwen-huaji.jpg" alt="Yuwen Huaji" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%AE%87%E6%96%87%E5%8C%96%E5%8F%8A%EF%BC%88%E8%AA%AA%E5%94%90%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E5%85%A8%E5%82%B3%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
